Subject: [PATCH] x86/tdx: a halt with interrupts off says so to the host

A TD cannot be seen to have interrupts off, so its halt tells the host
whether they are, and the host leaves a vCPU that halted with them off
halted until it is kicked. One routine served both the idle loop, which
halts with interrupts off and is to be woken by one, and the plain halt,
which leaves interrupts as they are. It told the host they were on, as the
idle loop needs.

A waiter for a spinlock takes the plain halt with interrupts off when the
lock is one taken with them off, and waits for the lock's releaser to kick
it. Told that interrupts were on, the host ended that halt for any pending
interrupt, which the waiter could not take: with a tick due every
millisecond the waiter then halted and came straight back for as long as it
waited, an exit each time. The plain halt now has a routine of its own that
says what the interrupts are. The idle loop's is as it was.

Linux-Version: 6.18.49
---
--- a/arch/x86/coco/tdx/tdx.c
+++ b/arch/x86/coco/tdx/tdx.c
@@ -468,6 +468,23 @@
 	raw_local_irq_enable();
 }
 
+/*
+ * The plain halt, which leaves interrupts as they are: the host is told
+ * which. tdx_halt() above is the idle loop's too, which halts with
+ * interrupts off and is to be woken by one, so it says they are on. A
+ * caller of the plain halt with interrupts off means it: a waiter for a
+ * lock halts so, for the lock's releaser to kick it (kvm_wait()). Told that
+ * interrupts were on, the host ended that halt for any interrupt that was
+ * pending, which the waiter could not take, and with a tick due every
+ * millisecond the waiter halted and came straight back for as long as it
+ * waited.
+ */
+static void __cpuidle tdx_halt_as_is(void)
+{
+	if (__halt(raw_irqs_disabled()))
+		WARN_ONCE(1, "HLT instruction emulation failed\n");
+}
+
 static int read_msr(struct pt_regs *regs, struct ve_info *ve)
 {
 	struct tdx_module_args args = {
@@ -1179,7 +1196,7 @@
 	 * in addition to having a reliable halt logic execution.
 	 */
 	pv_ops.irq.safe_halt = tdx_safe_halt;
-	pv_ops.irq.halt = tdx_halt;
+	pv_ops.irq.halt = tdx_halt_as_is;
 
 	/*
 	 * TDX intercepts the RDMSR to read the X2APIC ID in the parallel
